    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "HOLIDAY AIRLINES\nELECTRA\nYou are flying aboard an Electra, with a captain and crew who are thoroughly trained\nand experienced. There is little likelihood we will encounter a situation requiring\nemergency preparations but it is a good practice to be acquainted with the safety\nfeatures we have provided for you on this airplane. Follow the instructions of the\nflight crew.\nNO SMOKING\nWhen the \"NO SMOKING\" sign is off, you\nmay smoke while seated anywhere in the\ncabin or lounge area. Whenever the \"NO\nSMOKING\" sign comes on, however, all\nsmokes are to be extinguished.\nEMERGENCY EXITS\nCOCKPIT\nSEAT BELTS\nMove around as much as you like in the\ncabin while the seat belt sign is off. We\nsuggest, however, that you keep your seat\nbelt fastened while in your seats. Of\ncourse, seat belts must be fastened any\ntime the seat belt sign is on.\nMAIN\nCABIN\nDOOR\n(Stairs)\nSEAT BACKS\nDuring taxiing, takeoff and landing, each\nseatback in the aircraft must be in the up-\nright position.\nWINDOW\nEXIT\nWINDOW\nEXIT\nFLOTATION SEAT CUSHION\nThe cushion on which you are sitting is\ndesigned to keep you afloat. In the event\nof a water landing, grasp the cushion at\nthe rear, pull it forward and take it with you.\nIf seat marked \"Life Vest Under\nseat\" remove vest and take with\nyou instead of cushion.\nSERVICE\nDOOR\n(Slide)\nLOUNGE\nDOOR\n(Slide)\nSee reverse side\nfor instructions\nIF AN EMERGENCY LANDING SHOULD BE NECESSARY, OBSERVE THE FOLLOWING:\n• Loosen necktie and collar, remove spectacles and false teeth, and sharp articles from\npockets.\n• Adjust seat to full upright position and fasten seat belt securely.\n• Upon command \"Brace\" given by Stewardess, assume appropriate position.\nBRACE POSITIONS\nEVACUATION\nIf evacuation is ordered\nafter the landing, leave\nthrough the designated win-\ndow or door exit shown on\nthis chart. Assemble with\nother passengers at the des-\nignated point, well clear of\nthe airplane.\nFORWARD FACING\nSEATS\nAFT AND SIDE\nFACING SEATS",
      "MAIN CABIN DOOR OPERATION\nHAND CRANK HERE\nTO OPEN DOOR\nTURN HAND CRANK\nPUSH STAIR OUT\nEXIT\nOPEN\n1\nTO OPEN DOOR FLIP THE\nRED GUARDED SWITCH UP\nSERVICE DOOR OPERATION\nEXIT\nT\nPULL HANDLE DOWN\n2\nLIFT TO RAISE DOOR\nALL THE WAY UP-\nSLIDE WILL EJECT AND\nINFLATE AUTOMATICALLY\n3\nIF SLIDE DOES MOT\nINFLATE AUTOMATICALLY\nJERK THIS HANDLE\nLOUNGE DOOR OPERATION\nEXIT\nHAND\nGRIP\nPULL\n1 COVER\n2\nPULL\nHANDLE\nSLIDE\n3\nREMOVE DOOR - SHOWN ABOVE\n4 LIFT FLAP - PULL HANDLE UP\nSTAND CLEAR - SLIDE WILL\nAUTOMATICALLY EJECT AND\nINFLATE FOR USE\nSTAND CLEAR\nOF THIS AREA\nWINDOW OPERATION\nPULL\nCOVER\n1\nPULL\nHANDLE\n2\nTHERE ARE 3 WINDOW EXITS IN\nTHE MAIN CABIN\n3\nREMOVE WINDOW\nHOLIDAY AIRLINES\n2\nAFTER DOOR IS OPEN\nPUSH STAIRS OUT\n4 AFTER\nINFLA-\nTION\nCOMPLETE\nJUMP DOWN\nSLIDE\n5\nAFTER INFLATION COMPLETE -\nJUMP DOWN SLIDE\n4 CLIMB OUT WINDOW\nA FAST WAY OUT THE WINDOW IS\nONE LEG FIRST, THEN HEAD AND\nBODY FOLLOWED BY OTHER LEG.\nREV. 1-15-72"
